{"nodes":[{"id":"9f26f662240e01fd","type":"text","text":"Recurrent\n\n循环的","x":50,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120},{"id":"bccfdc96d9631503","type":"text","text":"convolutional\n\n卷积","x":330,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"443796679c7c1f77","type":"text","text":"self-respect\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A feeling of pride and confidence in oneself; a sense of one’s own worth or value.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 自尊  \n4) **Example sentence**: Most of us strive for self-respect — to see ourselves in a positive light, to be proud of who we are.","x":610,"y":50,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"85ac05e21491746c","type":"text","text":"undermine\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Verb  \n2) **English definition**: To weaken or damage something, especially someone’s confidence, authority, or feelings, often gradually or insidiously.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 削弱；损害；暗中破坏  \n4) **Example sentence**: Any comments or experiences that undermine those feelings of self-worth can be uncomfortable.","x":50,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"45aa5cd8bc91fc10","type":"text","text":"perception\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The way in which something is regarded, understood, or interpreted, often based on sensory experience or mental awareness.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 感知；认知；看法  \n4) **Example sentence**: \"Perception D.\" (The original sentence is incomplete, but a full example: \"Her perception of the situation changed after learning the truth.\")","x":330,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"49a5cc4526688794","type":"text","text":"citation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: A reference to a source (such as a book, article, or legal case) that provides authority or evidence for a statement or claim.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 引用；引证  \n4) **Example sentence**: *Citation B* refers to the second source listed in the bibliography.","x":610,"y":190,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"b6859ac9f45b5928","type":"text","text":"imitation\n\n1) **Part of speech**: Noun  \n2) **English definition**: The act of copying or reproducing something, often as a less authentic or inferior version.  \n3) **Chinese translation**: 模仿；仿制品  \n4) **Example sentence**: *imitation C.* (This suggests \"imitation\" is used as a label or category, likely meaning a copy or replica of type C.)","x":50,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"1"},{"id":"085b47fec20196fe","type":"text","text":"foolish\n\n1) Part of speech: Adjective  \n2) English definition: Lacking good sense, judgment, or wisdom; unwise.  \n3) Chinese translation: 愚蠢的；不明智的  \n4) Example sentence: It was foolish of him to go out in the rain without an umbrella.","x":330,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"fc06e4b1b1ab9ca7","type":"text","text":"interpreting\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Verb (gerund/present participle)  \n2) **Chinese translation:** 解读 / 诠释  \n3) **Example sentence:** She kept interpreting his silence as a sign of disapproval.","x":610,"y":330,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"4"},{"id":"8966ac0e444ac23b","type":"text","text":"term\n\n1) Part of speech: noun  \n2) Chinese translation: 术语；说法  \n3) Example sentence: The term for this way of thinking is personalisation.","x":50,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"d6094b883bfc9411","type":"text","text":"quotations\n\nBased on the context provided (the fragment \"quotations B\"), here is the definition:\n\n1) **Part of speech:** Noun (plural)\n2) **Chinese translation:** 引用/报价 (bàojià) — specifically referring to price quotes or estimates in a business or financial context.\n3) **Example sentence:** \"Please send us your latest quotations for product B.\"","x":330,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"color":"2"},{"id":"ce70f6230dd761f2","type":"text","x":610,"y":470,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"at work\n\n短语，起作用","color":"2"},{"id":"d0c17ed99dd591f4","type":"text","x":50,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"accounting for\n\nBased on the context provided (which appears to be a fragment, likely from a sentence like \"X is responsible for accounting for C\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Phrasal verb (prepositional verb)\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 解释；说明；占（比例）；对…负责\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **Meaning 1 (To explain or give a reason):** The manager had to **account for** the missing funds. (经理必须**解释**资金丢失的原因。)\n    *   **Meaning 2 (To constitute a specified portion):** The service sector **accounts for** over 60% of the country's GDP. (服务业**占**该国GDP的60%以上。)\n    *   **Meaning 3 (To be responsible for):** Each employee is **accounting for** their own time sheet. (每位员工都要**对**自己的考勤表**负责**。)","color":"2"},{"id":"213bb1a50c576684","type":"text","x":330,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interfering with\n\nBased on the context provided (only the phrase \"interfering with\"), here is the definition:\n\n1)  **Part of speech:** Verb phrase (present participle of \"interfere with\")\n2)  **Detailed Chinese translation:** 干涉；妨碍；干扰；介入（并阻碍）\n3)  **Example sentence for each meaning:**\n    *   **干涉 (to meddle):** Stop **interfering with** my personal life.\n    *   **妨碍 (to hinder/obstruct):** The storm is **interfering with** our travel plans.\n    *   **干扰 (to disrupt):** Please don't **interfere with** the machine while it's running.","color":"1"},{"id":"65c6c288b4191468","type":"text","x":610,"y":610,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"interpretations\n\nHere is the concise definition for \"interpretations\" based on the provided context:\n\n1) **All meanings for the word:**\n   - The action of explaining or understanding the meaning of something.\n   - A particular way of performing or presenting something (e.g., a piece of art or music).\n\n2) **Chinese translation for each meaning:**\n   - 解释；理解；解读\n   - 演绎；表演方式\n\n3) **Example sentence (using the original sentence):**\n   - \"When you find yourself taking a situation personally, try to think of other **interpretations** that are less focused on you — especially in the sense of saying anything deep or __(17)__ about you.\""},{"id":"2f692edf52dc2e8d","type":"text","x":50,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"feedback\n\nBased on the context provided (the sentence \"feedback C.\"), the word \"feedback\" is likely being used in a technical or systematic sense, possibly as a label or category. Here is the definition:\n\n**Feedback**  \n1) **Meaning**: Information about reactions to a product, a person's performance of a task, etc., used as a basis for improvement; or the return of a portion of the output of a system to the input, especially in electronics or cybernetics.  \n2) **Chinese translation**: 反馈；回馈  \n3) **Example sentence**: *The system uses feedback to adjust its output.* (The original sentence \"feedback C.\" is too brief to serve as a full example, but it suggests a category or label, e.g., \"Feedback C\" as a type of feedback.)","color":"2"},{"id":"04d86d117e682750","type":"text","x":330,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"nnovate\n\nBased on the context provided, here is the definition:\n\n1) **Meaning**: To introduce something new; to make changes in something established, especially by introducing new methods, ideas, or products. (Note: \"nnovate\" appears to be a typo for \"innovate.\")\n2) **Chinese translation**: 创新；革新\n3) **Example sentence**: innovate B. (This sentence is incomplete, but it suggests applying innovation to \"B,\" which could represent a product, process, or field.)","color":"2"},{"id":"f79b2b9a68892cd8","type":"text","x":610,"y":750,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"springs to mind\n\n浮现在脑海中","color":"2"},{"id":"ea432611da8eca57","type":"text","x":50,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"dusty\n\n布满灰尘的","color":"4"},{"id":"b300b618ac36a387","type":"text","x":330,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"rather like\n\n和...颇为相像","color":"4"},{"id":"56fd3000cb777a2d","type":"text","x":610,"y":890,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"startlingly\n\n惊人地","color":"4"},{"id":"7fa7536cf331dc4c","type":"text","x":50,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"commissioned\n\n受委托","color":"4"},{"id":"7cd5843e1f841a6f","type":"text","x":330,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"branches\n\n树枝\n分支，这里指分店","color":"4"},{"id":"e013898d6d93996d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1030,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"hive\n\n蜂巢\nzh-CN"},{"id":"9a3402282efcb6ce","type":"text","x":50,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"multitude\n\n众多\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"2085bd28a85f0a51","type":"text","x":330,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"entrepreneurs\n\n企业家\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"492ecde1bceb106d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1170,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"justify\n\n辩解\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"9fa300fda9df541c","type":"text","x":50,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"overlooked\n\n被忽视\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"eb37f5f95fe5a332","type":"text","x":330,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"underappreciated\n\n被低估\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"81886f7e5a4c8332","type":"text","x":610,"y":1310,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"impose\n\n强加\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"b87547bf4e8e4ba8","type":"text","x":50,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"disputed\n\n有争议\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"32b3cea52608c794","type":"text","x":330,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"flaws\n\n缺陷\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"e55aa437c699da8d","type":"text","x":610,"y":1450,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"campaign\n\n活动\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"57317b465bb21089","type":"text","x":50,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"memberships\n\n会员资格\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"1b58c1049ed74755","type":"text","x":330,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"confidential\n\n保密\nzh-CN","color":"1"},{"id":"b6a6ac8e72154a0f","type":"text","x":610,"y":1590,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"facilitate\n\n方便\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"d2ade82cb99127b1","type":"text","x":50,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"cited\n\n引用\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"424b7e8ea369ce9c","type":"text","x":330,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"outright\n\n直接\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"d30bf0c20d5e2b92","type":"text","x":610,"y":1730,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"landscape\n\n景观、格局\nzh-CN","color":"4"},{"id":"eb75d8b1507c0a30","type":"text","x":50,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"leveraging\n\n利用\nzh-CN","color":"2"},{"id":"4dfb540b97685472","type":"text","x":330,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"retains\n\n保留\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"d6e944bc20011934","type":"text","x":610,"y":1870,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"transparency\n\n透明度\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"7655fc88bf37aa6b","type":"text","x":50,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"navigate\n\n导航\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"bae81edce4fd2897","type":"text","x":330,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"cautiously\n\n谨慎\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"6cbeb858d03c5931","type":"text","x":610,"y":2010,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"budgets\n\n预算\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"53391c933355afa1","type":"text","x":50,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"overemphasise\n\n过分强调","color":"3"},{"id":"0da160768e66e294","type":"text","x":330,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"excessively\n\n过度\nzh-CN","color":"3"},{"id":"9c335d569c2f8e3c","type":"text","x":610,"y":2150,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"terms\n\nterms\n<i:100>\n[ielts]\n\nn. 条件, 条款, 费用, 价钱, 关系, 地位, 交谊\n[经] 条件\n\n释义: n status with respect to the relations between people or groups\nn the amount of money needed to purchase something\nn a word or expression used for some particular thing\nn a limited period of time\nn (usually plural) a statement of what is required as part of an agreement\nn any distinct quantity contained in a polynomial\nn one of the substantive phrases in a logical proposition\nn the end of gestation or point at which birth is imminent\nn (architecture) a statue or a human bust or an animal carved out of the top of a square pillar; originally used as a boundary marker in ancient Rome\nv name formally or designate with a term","color":"3"},{"id":"00424ecc912b227d","type":"text","x":50,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"chaos\n\nchaos\n/'keiɒs/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 大混乱, 混沌\n[化] 混沌; 浑沌\n\n释义: n. a state of extreme confusion and disorder\nn. the formless and disordered state of matter before the creation of the cosmos\nn. (Greek mythology) the most ancient of gods; the personification of the infinity of space preceding creation of the universe\nn. (physics) a dynamical system that is extremely sensitive to its initial conditions","color":"3"},{"id":"bf0b2b6f88eb0823","type":"text","x":330,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"Disruptions\n\ndisruptions\n/disˈrʌpʃənz/\n\nn. 中断( disruption的复数形式 ); 分裂; 瓦解; 破坏\n\n释义: n. an act of delaying or interrupting the continuity\nn. a disorderly outburst or tumult\nn. an event that results in a displacement or discontinuity","color":"4"},{"id":"5065ef2d6eca105b","type":"text","x":610,"y":2290,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"meantime\n\nmeantime\n/'mi:ntaim/\n<r:1/n:99>\n[cet4 cet6 ky]\n\nn. 间隔时间, 其时\nadv. 其间\n\n释义: n the time between one event, process, or period and another\nr during the intervening time","color":"3"},{"id":"8a397a91ec168145","type":"text","x":50,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"congestion\n\ncongestion\n/kәn'dʒestʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[toefl ielts]\n\nn. 拥挤, 充血\n[计] 拥挤, 拥塞\n\n释义: n. excessive accumulation of blood or other fluid in a body part\nn. excessive crowding","color":"1"},{"id":"2a815df6da59801a","type":"text","x":330,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"segregation\n\nsegregation\n/.segri'geiʃәn/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 隔离, 偏析, 被隔离的部分, 种族隔离\n[化] 分离; 分凝; 离析; 偏析; 分聚\n\n释义: n. (genetics) the separation of paired alleles during meiosis so that members of each pair of alleles appear in different gametes\nn. a social system that provides separate facilities for minority groups\nn. the act of segregating or sequestering","color":"1"},{"id":"681ca202b8263799","type":"text","x":610,"y":2430,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"density\n\ndensity\n/'densiti/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 密度\n[化] 密度\n\n释义: n. the amount per unit size","color":"3"},{"id":"c4e9e8ecbf3bd3f3","type":"text","x":50,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"reduction\n\nreduction\n/ri'dʌkʃәn/\n<n:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nn. 减少, 缩影, 变化\n[化] 还原\n\n释义: n. any process in which electrons are added to an atom or ion (as by removing oxygen or adding hydrogen); always occurs accompanied by oxidation of the reducing agent\nn. the act of reducing complexity","color":"3"},{"id":"dd9b44af0d814cc2","type":"text","x":330,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fluidity\n\nfluidity\n/flu:'iditi/\n<n:100>\n\nn. 流动性, 流质, 流状\n[化] 流动性; 流度\n\n释义: n. the property of flowing easily\nn. a changeable quality","color":"3"},{"id":"af785ee5bc8129bc","type":"text","x":610,"y":2570,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"intervals\n\nintervals\n/'ɪntevl/\n\nn. [军事]间隔( interval的复数形式 ); 间隔时间; [数学]区间; （戏剧、电影或音乐会的）幕间休息\n\n释义: n. a definite length of time marked off by two instants\nn. a set containing all points (or all real numbers) between two given endpoints\nn. the distance between things","color":"3"},{"id":"748f520e7e086b65","type":"text","x":50,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"beloved\n\nbeloved\n/bi'lʌvd/\n<j:94/n:6>\n[cet4 ky ielts]\n\na. 心爱的\nn. 心爱的人\n\n释义: n. a beloved person; used as terms of endearment\ns. dearly loved","color":"3"},{"id":"2794b0f01e9134ed","type":"text","x":330,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"stage\n\nstage\n/steidʒ/\n<v:8/n:92>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky ielts]\n\nn. 阶段, 舞台, 场所, 戏剧, 站, 驿站, 级, 层, 脚手架\nvt. 上演, 表演, 筹划\nvi. 适于上演, 乘驿车旅行\n\n释义: n. a large platform on which people can stand and can be seen by an audience\nn. the theater as a profession (usually `the stage')\nn. a section or portion of a journey or course\nn. any scene regarded as a setting for exhibiting or doing something","color":"3"},{"id":"44ee207fec1a0b35","type":"text","x":610,"y":2710,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"blossomed\n\nblossomed\n/ˈblɔsəmd/\n\nv. （植物）开花( blossom的过去式和过去分词 ); 发展; 长成; 变得更加健康（或自信、成功）\n\n释义: imp. & p. p. of Blossom","color":"3"},{"id":"28fbb22cd7337039","type":"text","x":50,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"abruptly\n\nabruptly\n/ә'brʌptli/\n<r:100>\n\nadv. 突然地, 唐突地\n\n释义: r. quickly and without warning","color":"3"},{"id":"8ede0102ca8f35f4","type":"text","x":330,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"primary\n\nprimary\n/'praimәri/\n<j:76/n:24>\n[zk gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 最主要者, 原色\na. 主要的, 初期的, 根本的, 原始的, 首要的, 基本的\n[计] 初等量; 主要的; 一次的\n\n释义: n. a preliminary election where delegates or nominees are chosen\nn. one of the main flight feathers projecting along the outer edge of a bird's wing\nn. (astronomy) a celestial body (especially a star) relative to other objects in orbit around it\na. of first rank or importance or value; direct and immediate rather than secondary","color":"4"},{"id":"a4ff4dfed28874d8","type":"text","x":610,"y":2850,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"skyrocketed\n\nskyrocketed\n/ˈskaɪˌrɔkɪtid/\n\nv. 突升, 猛涨( skyrocket的过去式和过去分词 )\n\n释义: v shoot up abruptly, like a rocket","color":"3"},{"id":"4196716ddd53f3b7","type":"text","x":50,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"entertainment\n\nentertainment\n/.entә'teinmәnt/\n<n:100>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts]\n\nn. 娱乐, 款待, 娱乐表演\n\n释义: n. an activity that is diverting and that holds the attention","color":"4"},{"id":"7e134c51bbb8a404","type":"text","x":330,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"portable\n\nportable\n/'pɒ:tәbl/\n<j:94/n:6>\n[gk cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 可携带的, 可搬运的, 可移动的\n[计] 可移植的\n\n释义: n. a small light typewriter; usually with a case in which it can be carried\na. easily or conveniently transported\ns. of a motor designed to be attached to the outside of a boat's hull","color":"1"},{"id":"16c7c37439962605","type":"text","x":610,"y":2990,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"fencing\n\nfencing\n/'fensiŋ/\n<n:100>\n[toefl gre]\n\nn. 围墙, 剑术\n[法] 围栏, 买卖赃物, 辩论\n\n释义: n. the art or sport of fighting with swords (especially the use of foils or epees or sabres to score points under a set of rules)","color":"1"},{"id":"29d18de24b0af833","type":"text","x":50,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"facilities\n\nfacilities\n[ielts gre]\n\nn. 工具, 设施, 设备\n\n释义: n a building or place that provides a particular service or is used for a particular industry\nn skillful performance or ability without difficulty\nn a natural effortlessness\nn something designed and created to serve a particular function and to afford a particular convenience or service\nn a service that an organization or a piece of equipment offers you","color":"1"},{"id":"2daa8e5018c2c580","type":"text","x":330,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"relieve\n\nrelieve\n/ri'li:v/\n<v:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl]\n\nvt. 减轻, 救济, 解除, 使免除, 换...的班, 使得到调剂, 使不单调, 衬托, 使显著\nvi. 救济, 当替补投手, 呈鲜明突出\n\n释义: v. provide physical relief, as from pain\nv. free from a burden, evil, or distress\nv. take by stealing\nv. alleviate or remove (pressure or stress) or make less oppressive","color":"1"},{"id":"d7649c47f5d58e66","type":"text","x":610,"y":3130,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"foster\n\nfoster\n/'fɒstә/\n<j:45/v:55>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 收养的, 养育的\nvt. 养育, 抚育, 培养, 鼓励, 抱(希望)\n\n释义: n. United States songwriter whose songs embody the sentiment of the South before the American Civil War (1826-1864)\nv. promote the growth of\nv. bring up under fosterage; of children\nv. help develop, help grow","color":"1"},{"id":"0e9b5610a4a0b1d5","type":"text","x":50,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"vibrancy\n\nvibrancy\n/'vaibrәnsi/\n<n:100>\n[gre]\n\nn. 振动, 振响, 活力\n\n释义: n having the character of a loud deep sound; the quality of being resonant","color":"1"},{"id":"37cf3de6c65db137","type":"text","x":330,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"amateur\n\namateur\n/'æmәtә/\n<j:61/n:39>\n[gk cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\nn. 业余爱好者, 外行, 爱好者\n[电] 业余家\n\n释义: n. someone who pursues a study or sport as a pastime\nn. an athlete who does not play for pay\ns. engaged in as a pastime","color":"1"},{"id":"7b22688e612e3af7","type":"text","x":610,"y":3270,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"prominent\n\nprominent\n/'prɒminәnt/\n<j:100>\n[cet4 cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\na. 卓越的, 显著的, 突出的, 凸出的\n\n释义: s having a quality that thrusts itself into attention\ns conspicuous in position or importance","color":"1"},{"id":"56ecf3a69c24dc90","type":"text","x":50,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"generosity\n\ngenerosity\n/.dʒenә'rɒsiti/\n<n:100>\n[cet6 gre]\n\nn. 慷慨, 宽大\n\n释义: n. the trait of being willing to give your money or time\nn. acting generously","color":"1"},{"id":"52550ea33edddccc","type":"text","x":330,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"expenditures\n\nexpenditures\n/ɪks'pendɪtʃəz/\n\nn. 花费( expenditure的复数形式 ); 使用; （尤指金钱的）支出额; （精力、时间、材料等的）耗费\n\n释义: n. money paid out; an amount spent\nn. the act of spending money for goods or services\nn. the act of consuming something","color":"3"},{"id":"5542f626d267863b","type":"text","x":610,"y":3410,"width":260,"height":120,"text":"chip\n\nchip\n/tʃip/\n<v:8/n:92>\n[cet6 ky toefl ielts gre]\n\n**chip in**: 加入\n\nn. 屑片, 薄片, 碎片\nvt. 削, 切, 削成碎片, 使摔倒, 凿\nvi. 削下屑片\n[计] 孔屑; 组件; 晶片; 芯片\n\n释义: n. a triangular wooden float attached to the end of a log line\nn. a piece of dried bovine dung\nn. a thin crisp slice of potato fried in deep fat\nn. a small disk-shaped counter used to represent money when gambling","color":"1"}],"edges":[]}